<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36926" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔξαρμα</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ατος</span>, τό, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξαίρω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>rising, swelling,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Epid.</u>
				4.31
			</span></i>; of the <i>tragus</i> of the ear, <i><span class="en">
				Ruf.
				<u>Onom.</u>
				44
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>meridian height</i> or <i>elevation</i> of the heavenly
			bodies, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῦ ἡλίου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Str.
					2.1.18
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				1.1.21
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῦ πόλου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hipparch.
					1.3.6
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Gem.
				6.24
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Mar.</u>
				11
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ptol.
				<u>Alm.</u>
				2.3
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				6
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Tetr.</u>
				76
			</span></i>; opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντέξαρμα,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>Theol.Ar.</u>
				25
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῦ ἐξάρματος ὃ ἐξῆρται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.410f
				</span></i>
			.</div>
